 "details": {
  "title": "Don’t Get Around Much Anymore",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement, slow and straight at 66 in A (B for the trumpet), concert A3 to F5, the way Rod Stewart’s record takes it, six semitones lower. The trumpet rests while the guitar plays its run, answers the riff with the tune’s own rhythm on the riff’s chords, and comes in with the tune where the singer does. Over the guitar’s E7♯5 the pickup starts on C natural; there are two lines of its own where the voice rests before each bridge, two breaths in the bridge, and a closing line over the ending’s D minor 6, A major 9, D minor 6, falling to C♯ as the guitar’s last run begins.",
  "facts": [
   [
